Package: flocate
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Conflicts: locate, mlocate, plocate
Replaces: mlocate, plocate
Description: forensic locate - fast file index with metadata and change history
 flocate is a fork of plocate. It keeps plocate's trigram index and query
 speed and adds a forensic layer: updatedb stores per-file metadata (mode,
 owner, size, timestamps, optional xxh64/sha256 hash) and a history of what
 changed between runs inside the database. flocate-showdiff replays that
 history, compares two databases, or compares a database against a live
 directory tree.
 .
 The package replaces locate, mlocate and plocate: it provides the locate
 and updatedb commands through the alternatives system, ships a daily
 systemd timer and reads the usual /etc/updatedb.conf.
